 "about": "Accept and refuse vectors of contract v26's table source (T2.1b; design choices 1 and 12): Relation { source: Vec<String> } in place of each data request's table string and each schema table's source string, and multi-column keys in neighbors and lookup. Each vector names the $defs definition it is an instance of. Both loaders read them: the Python one (tests/test_t21b_contract_v26.py) validates each against sdm-contract-26.json, and the Rust one (sdm-contract's tests) deserializes each into the type of that name, an accepted one round-tripping to an equal value. A vector marked v25 is a v25 message, valid under sdm-contract-25.json, which v26 no longer reads (host and core ship together, decision H25). How many parts a dialect takes is the dialect's to refuse by name (rule relation), not the contract's, so no vector here holds a relation of no part or of more than three.",
